I've implemented the override: `resolveToken` now uses an explicitly passed token first, then `process.env.API_TOKEN`, and throws as before if neither is set. The full test suite passes (9 of 9). Nothing is committed; the three changed files are uncommitted in the working tree.

The repo has a hook that blocks changes to a recorded decision unless the brief says the user named that decision and said to override it. Your brief named §explicit-token and said the maintainer overrode it, so I went ahead.

## Full `git diff`
```diff
